# Implementation Plan - Self-Learning Dynamic Route Engine

This plan outlines the design and implementation of an automated route-discovery and learning engine. The system will track live bus GPS traces during trips, reconstruct the actual sequence of stops traversed, automatically register new route variants in the database, and update the graph engine dynamically.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **In-Memory and Postgres Fallback Support**: To keep the existing implementation safe, the database queries in `apps/backend/src/db/index.ts` will be updated to support loading stops, routes, and route mappings, ensuring that the self-learning functionality operates correctly in both live Postgres database mode and the mock `data.json` fallback mode.
> - **Self-Learning Trigger**: Trips will automatically complete and trigger route learning when the bus reaches within 200 meters of the final destination stop, or when manually triggered via a new debug endpoint.

