### Route Learning Engine

#### [NEW] [routeLearning.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/engine/routeLearning.ts)
- Implement location-tracking buffers to keep track of the sequence of stops visited by each active trip: `visitedStopsMap: Map<number, number[]>` (maps `tripId` to an array of `stopId`).
- Implement `recordLiveLocation(tripId: number, latitude: number, longitude: number, speed: number)`:
  - Find all stops close to the bus coordinate (distance <= 0.2 km).
  - If a stop is found, append its ID to the visited list for the trip (if it is different from the last visited stop).
  - If this stop is the final destination of the trip's scheduled route, trigger `completeTripAndLearnRoute(tripId)`.
- Implement `completeTripAndLearnRoute(tripId: number)`:
  - Fetch the sequence of visited stops.
  - If the trip has traversed fewer than 2 stops, ignore (no route can be learned).
  - Fetch all existing routes connecting the same Source and Destination.
  - Compare the traversed stop sequence with the sequences of all matching routes.
  - If no match is found:
    - Generate a new route code (e.g. `R_LKO_KAN_VAR_1`).
    - Generate a descriptive route name containing intermediate stops.
    - Insert the new route and its stop sequences (calculating prefix distances using the haversine formula) into the database.
    - Re-trigger `buildGraph()` to dynamically load the new route into the pathfinder.
    - Mark the trip as `'completed'` in the database.
  - Clean up tracking cache for the completed trip.

